__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Pipeline output and intermediate files.
output/
out/
_work/
cache/

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Local config overrides (may contain paths and API keys)
config.yaml
config.toml
.env

# Exported browser cookies. A cookies.txt holds live session tokens: committing
# one hands over the account. Needed here because the natural place to drop the
# file is the repo root, right next to the tool that consumes it.
#
# ``cookies`` without the .txt is yt-dlp's OWN cookie jar, which it rewrites
# into the CWD on every run. Tracked by the first two lines -- catch it here
# rather than discovering it as an untracked file that looks like a stray.
cookies
cookies.txt
*cookies*.txt
*[Cc]ookie*.jar
!requirements.txt

# Run logs and tooling scratch. ``.err`` is here because the web server's
# stderr redirect (wsrv.err) lands in the repo root next to wsrv.log and
# would otherwise show up as an untracked file.
*.log
*.err
.pytest_cache/
.openclaw-probe-out/
.workbuddy-ai/

# The transcript's "which video is this" stamp, kept by the Ajustes page
# (TRANSCRIPT_SOURCE_PATH in web/server.py). It is per-machine bookkeeping
# about a local run, not project state: the same reason ajustes.toml itself
# carries no API keys but does carry local paths. Committing it would ship one
# person's video URL to everyone who clones.
.ajustes-transcript-source

# Os provedores que o usuario adiciona pelo card "Meus provedores" (web/index.html
# -> POST /providers/save). Fica fora do git pelo mesmo motivo de ajustes.toml:
# e config local de quem rodou o painel, e um merge num arquivo que a pagina
# reescreve por inteiro seria conflito garantido a cada `git pull`. A tabela
# revisada e versionada continua sendo viralclipper/providers.py.
provedores-usuario.toml

# Local visual-test images (not part of the web UI)
web/1.jfif
web/2.jpg
web/3.jpg

# The hero preview clips (see web/index.html). Personal footage, out of the repo
# for the same reason as the images above. Missing one degrades that card back to
# the schematic placeholder, which is the designed behaviour — the page never
# depends on these files.
web/[0-9]*.mp4

# Cache of scrap thumbnails: third-party video frames downloaded so the result
# cards can show them. Rebuilt on demand, and not ours to redistribute -- so it
# stays out of the repo. Lives under web/ rather than output/ on purpose: the
# output tree is the clip library and must not collect other people's frames.
web/thumbs/

# Scratch: one-off debug scripts, preset previews and sample transcripts kept
# next to the repo while tuning. Not part of the tool.
_scratch/

# Snapshot of the .git directory that lost its packfiles on 2026-09-22.
# Kept on disk for reference until the history is confirmed unrecoverable.
.git-corrompido-*/

# Viral Clip Studio (Node/React chat app). It is a separate application living
# inside the repo: its dependency tree, its SQLite database and its credentials
# have nothing to do with the Python pipeline. Ignored individually rather than
# with a blanket `studio/` so the source, the .env.example and the README of the
# Studio stay tracked.
studio/node_modules/
studio/dist/
studio/data/
studio/.env
studio/*.log

# Configuracao de modelos de terceiros do Studio. O arquivo versionado usa
# ${VAR} para as chaves, entao nao carrega segredo — mas se alguem colar uma
# chave em texto plano para testar, ela nao pode ir junto. A variante local
# fica fora, e a versao ${VAR} entra.
.codebuddy/models.local.json
.codebuddy/settings.local.json

